IMPORT prelude

-- Geographical Indications Act 2014 (Singapore) -- what a geographical indication is and who may enforce it (ss 2, 3), the acts
-- an interested party may sue over (s 4), groundless threats (s 8), exceptions (ss 11 to 16), offences and their composition
-- (ss 24, 25, 29, 30, 59A(3), 73, 81), and registration: who may apply, the Schedule of categories, refusal, duration,
-- cancellation and transfer (ss 38, 40, 41, 50, 52, 53 and the Schedule).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GIA2014.txt. The deposit
-- labels itself "Informal Consolidation -- version in force from 1/8/2026"; the latest amendment shown is G.N. No. S 523/2026
-- (amendment of the Schedule, in force 1 August 2026). Part 6 is shown as amended by Act 34 of 2018 (wef 21 November 2022) and
-- Act 5 of 2025 (wef 9 March 2025). The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is column-shifted from s 38 onwards;
-- the section numbers here are the BODY's.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 5 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a producer, trader or
-- practitioner meets. Not encoded: remedies and delivery-up beyond their existence (ss 5 to 7), declarations (ss 9, 10), the
-- Registry's administration (ss 17 to 23, 26 to 28, 31 to 37), examination, opposition, qualification and limitation
-- procedure (ss 43 to 49, 48A), homonymous indications (s 42), border measures in Part 6 other than two penalties, evidence and
-- costs (ss 75 to 79), body-corporate liability (s 80), rules and transitional provisions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Geographical Indications Act 2014 -- protection`

§§ `2 -- definitions`

-- s 2(1): "geographical indication" means any indication used in trade to identify goods as originating from a place, provided
-- that (a) the place is a qualifying country or a region or locality in a qualifying country; and (b) a given quality, reputation
-- or other characteristic of the goods is essentially attributable to that place.
-- "qualifying country": (a) a member of the World Trade Organization; (b) a party to the Paris Convention; or (c) designated by
-- the Minister under s 83.
-- "interested party": "a producer of the goods, a trader of the goods, or an association of such producers or traders".
-- "trader": a person who sells the goods in Singapore or supplies them in Singapore for sale by another in Singapore.
GIVEN `a WTO member` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Paris Convention party` IS A BOOLEAN, `designated by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualifying country` IF
    `a WTO member` OR `a Paris Convention party` OR `designated by the Minister`

GIVEN `used in trade to identify goods as from a place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the place is in a qualifying country` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a quality, reputation or characteristic is essentially attributable to the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a geographical indication` IF
        `used in trade to identify goods as from a place`
    AND `the place is in a qualifying country`
    AND `a quality, reputation or characteristic is essentially attributable to the place`

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a producer of the goods`
    `a trader selling the goods in Singapore`
    `an association of producers or traders`
    `a consumer of the goods`
    `a competitor making other goods`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an interested party` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `a producer of the goods` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a trader selling the goods in Singapore` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an association of producers or traders` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 and the Schedule -- acts an interested party may sue over`

-- The Schedule (amended by S 523/2026): 1 Wines, 2 Spirits, 3 Beers, 4 Cheese, 5 Meat and meat products, 6 Seafood, 7 Edible oils,
-- 8 Non-edible oils, 9 Fruits, 10 Vegetables, 11 Spices and condiments, 12 Confectionery and baked goods, 13 Flowers and parts of
-- flowers, 14 Natural gum, 15 Coffee. (Tea, handicraft products and textiles are NOT listed; they are here as contrasts.)
DECLARE Category IS ONE OF
    Wines
    Spirits
    Beers
    Cheese
    `Meat and meat products`
    Seafood
    `Edible oils`
    `Non-edible oils`
    Fruits
    Vegetables
    `Spices and condiments`
    `Confectionery and baked goods`
    `Flowers and parts of flowers`
    `Natural gum`
    Coffee
    Tea
    `Handicraft products`
    Textiles

GIVEN `the category` IS A Category
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Schedule category` IF
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN Tea THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Handicraft products` THEN FALSE
    WHEN Textiles THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 4(2)(a): use on goods not from the place "in a manner which misleads the public as to the geographical origin";
-- (b) use that is unfair competition under Article 10bis of the Paris Convention;
-- (c), (d): for a WINE or SPIRIT indication, use on a wine (spirit) not from the place "whether or not" the true origin is
-- stated, the indication is translated, or it is accompanied by "kind", "type", "style" or "imitation" -- no misleading needed.
-- s 4(6): the same for a REGISTERED indication identifying "any agricultural product or foodstuff (other than a wine or a spirit)
-- belonging to a category of goods listed in the Schedule", used on goods "of the same category". s 3(2): s 4(6) to (9) apply
-- only to registered indications.
-- s 4(5), (9): (c), (d) and (6) do not apply to naming an INGREDIENT, if literally true as to the ingredient's origin and not
-- falsely representing that the whole product comes from there.
-- (Not encoded: s 4(3), (7), an indication literally true but falsely representing origin in another place.)
GIVEN `the category` IS A Category, `the indication is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `it identifies an agricultural product or foodstuff` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has protection without proof of misleading` IF
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN Wines THEN TRUE
    WHEN Spirits THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `the indication is registered` AND `is a Schedule category` `the category` AND `it identifies an agricultural product or foodstuff`

GIVEN `the category` IS A Category,
      `the indication is registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it identifies an agricultural product or foodstuff` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the goods used on are of the same category` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the goods originate in the indicated place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the use misleads the public as to origin` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the use is unfair competition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it names only an ingredient that truly comes from there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 applies to the use` IF
        `the use is unfair competition`
    OR  ((NOT `the goods originate in the indicated place`) AND `the use misleads the public as to origin`)
    OR  (    (NOT `the goods originate in the indicated place`)
         AND `the goods used on are of the same category`
         AND `has protection without proof of misleading` `the category` `the indication is registered` `it identifies an agricultural product or foodstuff`
         AND (NOT `it names only an ingredient that truly comes from there`))

§§ `8 -- groundless threats`

-- s 8(1): any aggrieved person may sue over a threat of s 4 proceedings, OTHER THAN threats about (a) applying the indication to
-- goods or to labelling or packaging material, or (b) importing goods so marked.
-- (3): the claimant gets relief "unless the defendant shows" the act is (or would be) a s 4 act; (4) even then, relief if "the
-- claimant shows that an exception under this Act applies"; (5) "mere notification" that an indication is registered, or that an
-- application has been made, is not a threat.
GIVEN `the threat concerns only applying the indication or importing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it was a mere notification of registration or application` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the threatener shows the act is a section 4 act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the threatened person shows an exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the threatened person is entitled to relief` IF
        (NOT `the threat concerns only applying the indication or importing`)
    AND (NOT `it was a mere notification of registration or application`)
    AND ((NOT `the threatener shows the act is a section 4 act`) OR `the threatened person shows an exception applies`)

§§ `11, 13, 15 -- uses excepted from section 4`

-- s 11 (all indications): s 4 does not apply to the use of an indication (a) "contrary to public policy or morality"; (b) "not
-- or has ceased to be protected in its country or territory of origin"; (c) identical with the common name of the goods in
-- Singapore; (d) identical with the customary name of a grape variety existing in Singapore as of 1 January 1995; (e) "not
-- registered under this Act, and which has fallen into disuse in its country or territory of origin".
-- s 13: a person's own name or predecessor's name in the course of trade, "except where the name is used in such a manner as to
-- mislead the public".
-- s 15(b) (registered indications only, by s 3(2)): an indication or term in it "that is the name of a plant variety or an
-- animal breed".
DECLARE ExceptionGround IS ONE OF
    `contrary to public policy or morality`
    `no longer protected in its country of origin`
    `the common name of the goods in Singapore`
    `a grape variety name customary in Singapore on 1 January 1995`
    `fallen into disuse in its country of origin`
    `the name of a plant variety or animal breed`
    `the user's own name, not used misleadingly`
    `the user's own name, used misleadingly`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A ExceptionGround, `the indication is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 is excluded on the ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `fallen into disuse in its country of origin` THEN NOT `the indication is registered`
    WHEN `the name of a plant variety or animal breed` THEN `the indication is registered`
    WHEN `the user's own name, used misleadingly` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `12, 16 -- prior users`

-- s 12(1) (wine or spirit indications) and s 16(1) (registered indications for other goods): s 4 does not apply to use by a
-- "qualified person" who (with predecessors) has "continuously used in Singapore" the indication for those or related goods
-- "either (a) for at least 10 years preceding" the date, "or (b) in good faith preceding that date". The date is 15 April 1994 in
-- s 12 and 1 January 2004 in s 16.
-- ss 12(3), 16(4): "qualified person" -- (a) a citizen of Singapore or an individual resident in Singapore; (b) a body corporate
-- incorporated in Singapore; (c) any other person with "a real and effective industrial or commercial establishment in Singapore".
DECLARE User IS ONE OF
    `a Singapore citizen`
    `an individual resident in Singapore`
    `a company incorporated in Singapore`
    `a foreign firm with a real and effective establishment in Singapore`
    `a foreign firm with no establishment in Singapore`

GIVEN `the user` IS A User
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualified person` IF
    CONSIDER `the user`
    WHEN `a foreign firm with no establishment in Singapore` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the category` IS A Category
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is wine or spirit` IF
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN Wines THEN TRUE
    WHEN Spirits THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the category` IS A Category
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the prior-user cut-off date` MEANS
    IF `is wine or spirit` `the category` THEN 19940415 ELSE 20040101

GIVEN `the user` IS A User,
      `the category` IS A Category,
      `the indication is registered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years of continuous use in Singapore before the cut-off` IS A NUMBER,
      `the use was in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prior-user exception applies` IF
        `is a qualified person` `the user`
    AND (`is wine or spirit` `the category` OR `the indication is registered`)
    AND (    `years of continuous use in Singapore before the cut-off` AT LEAST 10
         OR (`years of continuous use in Singapore before the cut-off` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the use was in good faith`))

§§ `14 -- five years to sue over a trade mark`

-- s 14(1): no action under s 4 over use of a trade mark containing an indication "may be brought after the expiry of 5 years
-- beginning immediately after the earlier of" (a) the date the use "has become generally known in Singapore"; (b) the date the
-- mark was actually registered, "if the trade mark has been published by that date". (2): not where the mark was used or
-- registered in bad faith.
-- Dates are YYYYMMDD numbers; five years is + 50000 (an inference about how to count a calendar period; 29 February ignored).
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the date use became generally known` IS A NUMBER,
      `the date the mark was registered` IS A NUMBER,
      `the mark was published by its registration date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date the five years run from` MEANS
    IF `the mark was published by its registration date`
    THEN `the lesser of` `the date use became generally known` `the date the mark was registered`
    ELSE `the date use became generally known`

GIVEN `the date use became generally known` IS A NUMBER,
      `the date the mark was registered` IS A NUMBER,
      `the mark was published by its registration date` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the date the action is brought` IS A NUMBER,
      `the mark was used or registered in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the action is time-barred` IF
        (NOT `the mark was used or registered in bad faith`)
    AND `the date the action is brought` GREATER THAN
            `the date the five years run from` `the date use became generally known` `the date the mark was registered` `the mark was published by its registration date` PLUS 50000

§§ `24, 25, 29, 30, 59A, 73, 81 -- offences`

-- s 24 false entries in or copies of the register: $50,000 or 5 years or both. s 25(1) falsely representing an indication as
-- registered, knowing or having reason to believe it false: a fine not exceeding $10,000 -- NO imprisonment. s 29 failing to obey
-- the Registrar's summons and s 30 refusing to give evidence: $2,000 or 3 months. s 59A(3) failing to give information to a
-- border officer: $6,000 or 6 months. s 73 obstructing a border officer: $15,000 or 12 months.
-- s 81(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount
-- of the maximum fine" and (b) $5,000. (Which offences are prescribed is left to regulations not retrieved.)
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `falsifying the register`
    `falsely representing an indication as registered`
    `disobeying a Registrar's summons`
    `refusing to give evidence to the Registrar`
    `failing to give information to a border officer`
    `obstructing a border officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `falsifying the register` THEN 50000
    WHEN `falsely representing an indication as registered` THEN 10000
    WHEN `disobeying a Registrar's summons` THEN 2000
    WHEN `refusing to give evidence to the Registrar` THEN 2000
    WHEN `failing to give information to a border officer` THEN 6000
    WHEN `obstructing a border officer` THEN 15000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `falsifying the register` THEN 60
    WHEN `falsely representing an indication as registered` THEN 0
    WHEN `disobeying a Registrar's summons` THEN 3
    WHEN `refusing to give evidence to the Registrar` THEN 3
    WHEN `failing to give information to a border officer` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing a border officer` THEN 12

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition may collect` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

-- s 25(2): use in Singapore of "registered", or any word or symbol importing registration, "is deemed to be a representation as
-- to registration under this Act unless it is shown that the reference is to registration elsewhere than in Singapore and that the
-- geographical indication is in fact so registered for the goods in question".
GIVEN `the indication is registered in Singapore for the goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `shown to refer to registration outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in fact so registered there for the goods` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reason to believe it false` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the word registered is a section 25 offence` IF
        (NOT `the indication is registered in Singapore for the goods`)
    AND (NOT (`shown to refer to registration outside Singapore` AND `in fact so registered there for the goods`))
    AND `knew or had reason to believe it false`

§§ `38, 40, 41 -- who may apply, and what may not be registered`

-- s 38: entitled to apply -- (a) a person carrying on an activity as a producer in the geographical area specified, for the goods
-- specified; (b) an association of such persons; (c) a competent authority having responsibility for the indication.
-- s 40(1): only for goods within one or more Schedule categories.
DECLARE Applicant IS ONE OF
    `a producer in the area for those goods`
    `an association of such producers`
    `a competent authority for the indication`
    `a trader of the goods`
    `a producer outside the area`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for registration` IF
    CONSIDER `the applicant`
    WHEN `a producer in the area for those goods` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an association of such producers` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a competent authority for the indication` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 41(1): must not be registered -- (a) not a "geographical indication" within s 2; (b) goods outside the Schedule; (c) contrary
-- to public policy or morality; (d) not or no longer protected in its country of origin; (e) identical to the common name of the
-- goods in Singapore; (f) contains a plant variety or animal breed name "and is likely to mislead the consumer as to the true
-- origin of the product".
GIVEN `it is a geographical indication` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the category` IS A Category,
      `contrary to public policy or morality` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `protected in its country of origin` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `identical to the common name of the goods in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contains a plant variety or breed name and is likely to mislead` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `registration is barred by section 41(1)` IF
        (NOT `it is a geographical indication`)
    OR  (NOT `is a Schedule category` `the category`)
    OR  `contrary to public policy or morality`
    OR  (NOT `protected in its country of origin`)
    OR  `identical to the common name of the goods in Singapore`
    OR  `contains a plant variety or breed name and is likely to mislead`

-- s 41(4), (6): must not be registered where it would cause confusion with a qualifying earlier trade mark (registered or applied
-- for in good faith, or used in good faith, before the GI application), or a well known mark where registration "is liable to
-- mislead consumers". (7): the Registrar "may, in the Registrar's discretion" register anyway if the proprietor "(a) consents" or
-- "(b) fails to give notice ... of the proprietor's opposition" under s 45(2). So without a bar the Registrar MAY register; this
-- is not a duty to.
GIVEN `it conflicts with a qualifying earlier trade mark` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the proprietor consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the proprietor failed to oppose in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trade mark bars registration` IF
        `it conflicts with a qualifying earlier trade mark`
    AND (NOT `the proprietor consented`)
    AND (NOT `the proprietor failed to oppose in time`)

§§ `50, 52, 53 -- duration, cancellation and transfer`

-- s 50: registered "for a period of 10 years from the date of registration", renewable "for further periods of 10 years in respect
-- of each renewal". s 51(4): a renewal "takes effect from the expiry of the previous registration". (YYYYMMDD + 100000 per decade.)
GIVEN `the date of registration` IS A NUMBER, `the number of renewals` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the registration expires on` MEANS
    `the date of registration` PLUS 100000 TIMES (`the number of renewals` PLUS 1)

-- s 52(1)(a): cancellation by the Registrar on the registrant's application -- (5) rights cease from the date of cancellation.
-- s 52(2) grounds on another person's application: (a) registered in breach of s 41; (b) obtained fraudulently or by
-- misrepresentation -- (6) "deemed never to have been registered"; (c) ceased to be protected at origin; (d) failure to maintain
-- any commercial activity or interest in Singapore; (e) become the common name through lack of activity -- (7) rights cease from
-- the date of the application for cancellation, or an earlier date if the ground existed then.
DECLARE CancellationGround IS ONE OF
    `the registrant's own application`
    `registered in breach of section 41`
    `obtained by fraud or misrepresentation`
    `no longer protected at origin`
    `no commercial activity in Singapore`
    `become the common name through inactivity`

DECLARE CancellationEffect IS ONE OF
    `deemed never registered`
    `rights end on the date of cancellation`
    `rights end on the application date or an earlier date the ground existed`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A CancellationGround
GIVETH A CancellationEffect
`the effect of cancellation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the registrant's own application` THEN `rights end on the date of cancellation`
    WHEN `registered in breach of section 41` THEN `deemed never registered`
    WHEN `obtained by fraud or misrepresentation` THEN `deemed never registered`
    OTHERWISE `rights end on the application date or an earlier date the ground existed`

-- s 53(2): the registration "must not be transferred to another person unless that person (a) is entitled to file an application
-- ... under section 38; and (b) consents".
GIVEN `the transferee` IS A Applicant, `the transferee consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration may be transferred` IF
    `may apply for registration` `the transferee` AND `the transferee consents`
